                <h2>When to Use This SOP</h2>
<p>This guide applies to e-commerce teams with monthly ad budgets between $5,000 and $100,000. If your budget is smaller or larger, scale the ratios proportionally—the underlying logic remains the same.</p>
<hr />
<h2>Step 1: Set Your Overall Budget Framework</h2>
<p>Before allocating to specific platforms, establish your target ad spend as a percentage of revenue (ACoS or TACoS).</p>
<p><strong>Standard Benchmarks:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Cold Start Phase (0-3 months):</strong> Target ACoS 50%-80%, focus on testing</li>
<li><strong>Growth Phase (3-6 months):</strong> Target ACoS 30%-50%, optimize creatives and audiences</li>
<li><strong>Scaling Phase (6+ months):</strong> Target ACoS 15%-30%, maximize ROAS and scale</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Action Items:</strong></p>
<ol>
<li>Set a monthly budget cap in your ad accounts, then calculate your daily ceiling (monthly ÷ 30 × 1.2 for 20% buffer)</li>
<li>Divide total budget into "Testing Budget" and "Stabilized Budget": 40% testing in cold start, 20% in growth, 10% in scaling phase</li>
</ol>
<blockquote>
<p>Note: Keep testing budget separate from performance campaigns. Don't mix experimental and proven strategies in the same account structure.</p>
</blockquote>
<hr />
<h2>Step 2: Allocate Budget Across Platforms</h2>
<p>Allocate to platforms based on your store's growth stage. Adjust ratios based on your data.</p>
<h3>Budget Allocation Reference Table</h3>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Phase</th>
<th>Google Ads</th>
<th>Meta (FB/IG)</th>
<th>TikTok</th>
<th>Email/Retargeting</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Cold Start</td>
<td>35%</td>
<td>40%</td>
<td>10%</td>
<td>15%</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Growth</td>
<td>40%</td>
<td>35%</td>
<td>15%</td>
<td>10%</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Scaling</td>
<td>45%</td>
<td>30%</td>
<td>15%</td>
<td>10%</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p><strong>Platform Notes:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Google Ads:</strong> Best for capturing high-intent search traffic. Focus on brand/product keywords and Shopping ads (ideal for stores with large SKU catalogs)</li>
<li><strong>Meta:</strong> Excels at interest-based targeting and Lookalike audiences. Use UGC-style creatives for awareness and consideration. Start with single images and carousels during cold start</li>
<li><strong>TikTok:</strong> Lower CPMs currently, great for testing new creatives and reaching women aged 25-35. Creative quality requirements are higher here</li>
<li><strong>Retargeting:</strong> Average cart abandonment rates run 60%-80% on e-commerce sites. Retargeting budgets are small but often deliver the highest ROI</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>Step 3: Internal Budget Structure Per Platform</h2>
<p>Once budget reaches each platform, split it further within that platform.</p>
<h3>Google Ads Internal Breakdown</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Search Ads:</strong> 60% — brand + core product keywords</li>
<li><strong>Shopping Ads:</strong> 30% — upload product feed, optimize titles and images</li>
<li><strong>Display Ads:</strong> 10% — retargeting or interest-based reach</li>
</ul>
<h3>Meta Internal Breakdown</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Facebook Dynamic Feed:</strong> 50% — programmatic, auto-serve products users viewed but didn't purchase</li>
<li><strong>Instagram Stories:</strong> 20% — short, fast-paced creatives</li>
<li><strong>Facebook Dynamic Product Ads (DPA):</strong> 30% — best for stores with extensive SKU catalogs</li>
</ul>
<h3>TikTok Internal Breakdown</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>In-feed Ads:</strong> 80% — vertical video, hook viewers in the first 3-5 seconds</li>
<li><strong>TopView:</strong> 20% — cold start awareness testing</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>Step 4: Daily/Weekly Budget Adjustment SOP</h2>
<p>Budget allocation isn't set-and-forget. Adjust based on performance data.</p>
<h3>Daily Checks (5 minutes)</h3>
<ol>
<li>Verify each ad group is at or below 80% of daily budget</li>
<li>Pause any ad groups burning through budget with zero conversions</li>
<li>Flag any sudden spend spikes (e.g., one creative running unexpectedly at night)—investigate potential click fraud</li>
</ol>
<h3>Weekly Adjustments (30 minutes)</h3>
<ol>
<li>Pull ACoS/ROAS data for all platforms, compare to targets</li>
<li>Cut bottom 20% performers' budgets by 30% or pause and retest</li>
<li>Increase top 20% performers' budgets by 20%-50% (set campaign caps to prevent runaway spend)</li>
<li>Refresh test ad accounts with new creatives; retire any creatives older than 3 weeks with no conversions</li>
</ol>
<h3>Monthly Reviews (1 hour)</h3>
<ol>
<li>Compare this month vs. last month's CAC and LTV per channel</li>
<li>Reassess platform allocation ratios</li>
<li>Evaluate new platforms to test (Pinterest, Snapchat, etc.)</li>
</ol>
<hr />
<h2>Troubleshooting Quick Reference</h2>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Problem</th>
<th>Solution</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Google Ads not spending</td>
<td>Keywords may be underbidding or Quality Score below 6. Increase bids 10%-20%</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Meta CTR below 1%</td>
<td>Change creative direction; test UGC-style or comparison creatives</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>High TikTok conversion costs</td>
<td>Prioritize 5-second completion rate; ensure the hook is in the first 3 seconds</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Retargeting has great ROAS but low volume</td>
<td>Expand Pixel coverage; increase touchpoints before first conversion</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Budget depleted unexpectedly</td>
<td>Check for creative blowup; set ad group budget caps</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<hr />
<h2>Action Checklist for Your Team</h2>
<p>After reading this guide, your team should complete these items immediately:</p>
<ul>
<li>[ ] Confirm monthly total ad budget and daily ceilings</li>
<li>[ ] Split budget across Google Ads, Meta, and TikTok per the ratios above</li>
<li>[ ] Verify Shopping feed is live in Google Ads</li>
<li>[ ] Enable Dynamic Product Ads in Meta</li>
<li>[ ] Set up daily spend alerts (trigger at 80% of daily budget)</li>
<li>[ ] List 3 new creatives to test this week</li>
</ul>
<p>Once these checkpoints are complete, your budget allocation framework is live. Adjust weekly based on data, and within 2-3 months you'll develop stable ratios tailored to your products and audience.</p>
